# Test: the X-Ze-Version banner obeys the hide-version leaf on both HTTP servers
# VALIDATES: spec-mgmt-version-header-suppress AC-1 (the web server omits the
# banner when hidden), AC-2 (the looking glass omits it), AC-3 (a config that
# writes nothing keeps it), AC-4 (the other security headers survive), AC-5 (no
# Server banner replaces it). One daemon serves both HTTP surfaces, and the two
# runs share one configuration text apart from the hide-version leaf.
# PREVENTS: one server honoring the toggle while the other still publishes the
# exact build, a guard that takes the other security headers down with the
# version, and the opt-in hardening becoming the default.
# The web server needs blob storage and a user, so the fixture runs `ze init`
# and writes a system block before it starts either daemon.

option=timeout:value=120s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture plugin/version-header-suppress:timeout=120s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: both servers send the version banner by default
expect=stderr:contains=OK: hide-version takes the banner off both servers
expect=stderr:contains=OK: the other security headers survive suppression
expect=stderr:contains=OK: neither server sends a Server banner
